o as \"the bare-arsed Ferdinand\", Ferdinand being a reference to the German Heavy Ferdinand/Elefant Tank Destroyer.","LocalizedString":"The SU-76, also known as Samokhodnaya Ustanovka 76, was a Soviet self-propelled gun used during and after WWII. A lengthened and widened version of the T-70 light tank chassis was used as a base and due to its simple construction it was the second most produced Soviet armored vehicle in WWII, after the T-34. It was liked by the crews for its reliability and ease of use, but the steering was sometimes considered difficult and due to its light armor it was sometimes referred to as \"the bare-arsed Ferdinand\", Ferdinand being a reference to the German Heavy Ferdinand/Elefant Tank Destroyer."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","isInPermanentPool":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment"],"hasDeployment":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Tank_Heavy_Move_Fx'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Tank_Heavy_Move_Fx.0"},"soundMoveToFrontline":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Tank_Heavy_Move_Fx'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Units/Tank_Heavy_Move_Fx.0"},"soundAttack":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Heavy_artillery_2'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/ExplosionSoundPack/ExplosionSounds/Wavs/Heavy_artillery_2.0"},"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Huge'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Huge.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/t_su_76.t_su_76","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::Bot","artist":"Mitchell Nolte","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/SU-76.SU-76","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":517.0},"historyPhotoSource":"https://ww2db.com","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_unit_su_76_photo","SourceString":"Russian SU-76 self-propelled gun and its crew, date unknown.","LocalizedString":"Russian SU